// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/lab/job_kind.t27 -- the lab gate as one more job kind of the network: LAB_GATE, run by any T27 OS
; node, admitted by k-of-n agreement, credited in test-network XP
; Issue gHashTag/t27#11043 (lab epic #11040, T27 OS epic #11037). Owner direction, 2026-10-19: the lab is
; mobile and built into T27 OS, and it pays for useful work -- in test-network XP now -- so that users hand
; their machines to the network. The network pays the node; nobody asks a host for capacity. A lab gate
; (build, suite, seal currency, the t27b verdict, the analog reference run) stops being a place and becomes
; a job type.
; --
; Reused, not restated. Every rule below that is not about gates or about T27 OS nodes is read from where
; it already lives:
; - network/job_rules.t27: AGREE_FIELDS (two receipts agree when the commit, the three roots and the totals
;   are byte-equal; the binaries' hashes may differ), results_agree, receipt_auth's AUTH_* codes, and
;   quorum_verdict with its QV_* words (QUORUM, BELOW_QUORUM, NO_VOTE, SPLIT);
; - network/quorum.t27: the admission rule 2M > N + F, quorum_admits, safe_m, one vote per operator;
; - hosting/proof.t27: the k-of-n of one job's replicas (REPLICAS_K 2, tiebreak up to REPLICAS_MAX 3) and
;   which side of an agreed job a receipt is on; hosting/sybil.t27: the anchored form of the same verdict,
;   and what a slash forfeits; hosting/placement.t27: whether a node may take a replica now (it is up, not
;   suspended, has a free slot) and that a retry never goes back to a node that already held the gate;
; - hosting/host.t27: the trust tiers and which workload a tier may receive; hosting/credit.t27: the credit
;   per receipt, one row per (node, job, kind), and the settlement that stays off; hosting/statement.t27:
;   the ledger rows (kind and amount), the balance, the epoch;
; - verified/payout.t27: EXECUTOR_FEE and VERIFIER_FEE, receipt_award (an agreeing, fresh receipt earns its
;   fee, a disagreeing one is slashed), CREDIT_TRANSFERABLE false;
; - jobs/network_job.t27: CREDIT_IS_TEST and the challenge window; trinet/node-work-credit.t27: the
;   per-job rate REWARD_PER_JOB_MTRI; t27f/petal_menu.t27: the home of T27 OS, whose petal this card's
;   reward is shown under.
; Not decided here: whose receipts reach the coordinator, the signatures and the sockets (the node agent
; and the coordinator), the toolchain pins and the sandbox a gate runs in (hosting/toolchain.t27), and the
; anchor, canaries, probation and per-epoch cap of hosting/sybil.t27, which are the ledger writer's second
; gate on every credit, gate credits included. The amounts below are the amounts before that gate.
; --
; The job. A LAB_GATE job is two inputs: a commit sha (40 lowercase hex digits, never an abbreviation, a
; path or an option) and a gate id from a CLOSED enum of five gates. The gate command is the enum's own
; line (LJK_GATE_COMMANDS), a plain word list this card checks (ljk_command_plain); it never comes from
; pull-request text, and a node is never sent a command at all, only the id. A gate id outside the enum is
; refused by the coordinator before any node is asked (ljk_offer judges the gate first).
; --
; Trust. A gate is a deterministic job with pinned inputs: no secret, no personal data (LJK_HOLDS_SECRET
; and LJK_HOLDS_PERSONAL are false for every gate). So it is a PUBLIC job: hosting/host.t27 `eligible`
; admits it to the lowest trust tier, and any node may run it. A node is never handed a GitHub token or
; any other credential: the offer is the sha, the gate id and the challenge (LJK_OFFER_FIELDS) and
; nothing else, the node returns a signed verdict, and the coordinator publishes it. A verdict is the
; corpus receipt's layout (verified/corpus_receipt.t27) whose commit is the sha and whose nonce is the
; challenge of the offer. The coordinator draws one challenge per offer, so a verdict answers the one gate
; that was asked; that draw is the coordinator's, not this card's.
; --
; Placement of a T27 OS node. A node is a desktop, a laptop or a phone, and it reports its cores, its free
; disk, whether it is charging and whether its link is unmetered. A gate has a class, light, medium or
; heavy. The floors (cores, free disk) and the power and link needs are the owner's parameters, a choice
; and not a measurement of any gate; changing them is a pull request like any other. The rule, as pure
; functions (ljk_node_takes, ljk_offer): a node takes a gate only if its class may take that gate class
; at all, it has the cores and the free disk the class needs, and its power state and link are what the
; class needs. A desktop takes any class it has the room for. A laptop takes light work on battery and
; medium or heavy work only while charging. A phone takes only light gates, only while charging, only on
; an unmetered link.
; --
; Agreement and retry. The receipts of one gate agree when results_agree holds (AGREE_FIELDS). The next
; move is a function of hosting/proof.t27's verdict (ljk_next): two receipts that agree admit the gate;
; two that do not are a split round (quorum_verdict answers QV_SPLIT) and the gate is retried on one more
; node, up to REPLICAS_MAX; a retry that makes a majority admits the gate; with no majority the gate is
; void. A slash needs an admitted gate: only then is there a side to be on (payout.t27 receipt_award), so a
; 1-1 split slashes nobody and the minority of a 2-1 round is slashed. Votes are independent operators
; (network/quorum.t27): two nodes of one operator are one vote and the second earns nothing. The honest
; ceiling stays proof.t27's: agreement shows that k keys reported the same bytes, and k keys can be one
; person; the anchored verdict of hosting/sybil.t27 is the stricter judgment, and ljk_next takes either.
; --
; Reward. XP is test-network credit and is not a new ledger: a row is a hosting/statement.t27 row (kind
; EXECUTOR_FEE for the first agreeing receipt, VERIFIER_FEE for a later one or when a known answer already
; existed, or a slash) whose amount is the gate class's XP weight times the per-job rate of
; hosting/credit.t27, so one XP is REWARD_PER_JOB_MTRI of test credit and a light gate pays what a shard
; pays today. A disagreeing receipt of an admitted gate is slashed; a receipt that is not authentic for its
; offer, or answers a stale challenge, earns nothing and is not slashed. network/pool.t27's split of a
; job's pool is not used: a gate has no escrow and no emission schedule is set for it, the reason
; hosting/credit.t27 gives for a shard's per-receipt rate. CREDIT_IS_TEST stays true, SETTLEMENT_ENABLED
; stays false, credit is not transferable and no token value is claimed.
; --
; The home. T27 OS shows a level and a streak read off the same rows: a level is LJK_LEVEL_XP XP of balance
; (credits less slashes, statement.t27 balance_after_entry), a streak is the run of epochs (one day each,
; statement.t27) with at least one credited gate. A streak changes no amount. The card belongs to the
; Y YIELD petal of t27f/petal_menu.t27 (LJK_HOME_PETAL).
; ASCII only (L3).
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module LabJobKind;

